130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (The compounding effect of overlapping crises has only intensified in the current biennium. A UN Department of Economic and Social Affairs report presented to ECOSOC noted that deepening geopolitical fragmentation and conflict are jeopardizing decades of development progress, with the escalation of conflict in the Middle East triggering a significant shock to an already fragile global economy, with developing countries absorbing the consequences through higher energy costs, disrupted trade, food price volatility, and worsening debt sustainability. Post-conflict states therefore face a uniquely difficult recovery arithmetic: reconstruction needs measured in the hundreds of billions of dollars, domestic revenue bases shattered by war, and access to concessional international capital that remains, in the words of UN and partner agencies, 'too often missed' at the moment it is most needed. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Financing Reconstruction: Bridging the Gap Between Relief and Development Finance )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (A central obstacle to post-conflict recovery is the financing gap between short-term humanitarian relief, which is well-funded and rapidly deployable, and long-term development finance, which is typically unavailable to fragile and conflict-affected markets that fall below investment grade. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (2 )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Within this architecture, ECOSOC does not have an operational or peacekeeping mandate; its comparative advantage lies in convening financing conversations, setting normative economic and social policy, and coordinating the specialized agencies and international financial institutions \(the World Bank Group and the International Monetary Fund\) that carry out reconstruction and recovery work on the ground. It is this convening and coordinating function that the Council is being asked to exercise on the present agenda item. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
