/P 98 0 R
/E (manufacturing has highlighted the importance of balancing national security concerns with the need to preserve an open, stable, and predictable global trading system. Governments alone cannot address these challenges; meaningful progress requires cooperation with international financial institutions, the private sector, and multilateral organizations to develop sustainable investment frameworks, encourage responsible resource utilization, and ensure that national economic policies support long-term global economic resilience rather than creating disproportionate costs for other economies. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (The growing concentration of critical resources and strategic technologies further illustrates the need for coordinated international action. Global production of semiconductors, rare earth elements, lithium, cobalt, and other strategic materials remains concentrated within a limited number of countries, increasing the risk of supply disruptions and market volatility. Similarly, competition over digital infrastructure, clean energy technologies, and advanced )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
