/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (The widespread destruction of health infrastructure severely undermines every other dimension of post-conflict recovery. In Gaza, more than half of hospitals remain non-functional and over 90 percent of the territory's broader infrastructure has been affected, health-system reconstruction is now a precondition for economic activities rather than a future positive. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (Beyond conflict and climate-related pressures, food security is increasingly influenced by national trade and resource policies that extend far beyond domestic borders. Export restrictions on staple crops, fertilizers, and agricultural inputs, alongside disruptions to global supply chains and unequal access to strategic resources, can significantly amplify food insecurity in import-dependent economies. While such measures are often introduced to safeguard domestic interests, they may unintentionally increase price volatility, constrain market access, and undermine agricultural productivity in other regions. Strengthening international cooperation on transparent trade practices, sustainable resource management, and resilient agricultural supply chains is therefore essential to ensuring that national policy decisions do not disproportionately compromise global food security or hinder progress toward the Sustainable Development Goals. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
