/P 101 0 R
/E (As economies become increasingly interconnected, disruptions caused by unilateral trade measures, export restrictions, and unequal access to strategic resources can significantly hinder economic activity beyond national borders. Dependence on a limited number of suppliers for semiconductors, critical minerals, and energy has exposed vulnerabilities that can increase production costs, disrupt supply chains, and slow economic growth, particularly in developing economies. These challenges highlight ECOSOC's coordinating role in making sure everything is laid down perfectly - things ranging from international cooperation all the way to policy frameworks to minimize impacts that can cause such catastrophes. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
